The frontend's 13 Oct ask (FIXED2 „რა მოხდა" → „მოგვიანებით"):
- GET /updates/held → { held: [{ update_ref, title, detail, until }] }:
  the caller's held rows still ahead, soonest first, capped at 50. It uses
  the same WHERE as the held count (HELD_AND_STILL_REAL), and spends nothing.
- DELETE /updates/:ref/snooze: bring a held row back now (release_at = NOW()).
  400 for a bad ref; 404 when the row is not the caller's or not held for
  later.
Parameterised, with a timeout, scoped to the caller. Service tests, route
source tests, and the KINDS call-site count updated. FOR_FRONTEND has the
contract.

